dho:SeeingWhatIsGood a dho:Concept ;
    skos:altLabel "knowing what is good"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "truly knowing and seeing what is good for oneself, for another, and for both"@en,
        "attattha parattha ubhayattha yathābhūtaṁ jānāti passati"@pi .

dho:p-sn46.130-1.8 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.130 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.130:1.8" ;
    dho:textEn "It’s when a mendicant develops the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.130/en/sujato#sn46.130:1.8"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.5-1.7 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.5 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.5:1.7" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.5/en/sujato#sn46.5:1.7"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-9.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:9.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And what is the way in which the five hindrances become ten?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Katamo ca, bhikkhave, pariyāyo, yaṁ pariyāyaṁ āgamma pañca nīvaraṇā dasa honti?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:9.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-9.12 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:9.12" ;
    dho:textEn "This is the way in which the five hindrances become ten."@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ayaṁ kho, bhikkhave, pariyāyo, yaṁ pariyāyaṁ āgamma pañca nīvaraṇā dasa honti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:9.12"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-12.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:12.3" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "mettāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:12.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-13.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:13.3" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "karuṇāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:13.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-14.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:14.3" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "muditāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:14.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-15.2 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:15.2" ;
    dho:textEn "It’s when a mendicant develops the heart’s release by equanimity together with the awakening factors of mindfulness, investigation of principles, energy, rapture, tranquility, immersion,"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Idha, bhikkhave, bhikkhu upekkhāsahagataṁ satisambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ …pe…"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:15.2"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.54-15.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.54 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.54:15.3" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "upekkhāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.54/en/sujato#sn46.54:15.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-2.6 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:2.6" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "nirodhasaññāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:2.6"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.76-3.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.76 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.76:3.4" ;
    dho:textEn "and equanimity, which rely on seclusion, fading away, and cessation, and ripen as letting go."@en ;
    dho:textPi "nirodhasaññāsahagataṁ upekkhāsambojjhaṅgaṁ bhāveti vivekanissitaṁ virāganissitaṁ nirodhanissitaṁ vossaggapariṇāmiṁ."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.76/en/sujato#sn46.76:3.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-mn43 a dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    skos:prefLabel "MN 43 Mahāvedallasutta — The Great Elaboration"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Only the first absorption: its five factors (19.2-19.3), and that it gives up the five hindrances and possesses those five factors (20.2-20.4)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "Most of the dialogue: wisdom and consciousness (2-6), feeling, perception and consciousness (7-9), what purified mind consciousness can know and how it is understood with the eye of wisdom (10-11), the goal of wisdom and conditions for right view (12-14), states of existence (15-17), what the first absorption is (18), the five faculties (21-22), vital forces and death vs cessation (23-25), and the releases of the heart (26-37)." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-13"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/mn43/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.1 a dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.1 Himavantasutta — The Himalaya"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "The seven factors developed depending on and grounded on ethics (1.4), and the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (1.6, 1.12). The simile of dragons growing strong on the Himalayas (1.2-1.4; D22)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "The result 'acquiring great and abundant good qualities' (1.4, 1.13): kept in the simile's point (D22), not modelled as an outcome. The simile itself is encoded (1.2-1.4)." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.1/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.16 a dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.16 Tatiyagilānasutta — Sick (3rd)"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Mahācunda to the sick Buddha, at his request: the same statement as SN 46.14 (2.1-2.4); the Buddha concurs (2.5-2.6, 3.2)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "The setting (1.1-1.4). The Buddha's affirmation (2.5-2.6). The narrative of his recovery (3.3-3.4, with the Pali-only 'in that way that illness was abandoned', 3.4): narrated, not taught." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-15"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.16/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.26 a dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.26 Taṇhakkhayasutta — The Ending of Craving"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "The seven factors are the path that leads to the ending of craving (1.1, 1.4); the list (1.6); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.1, 2.5)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "The chain: as they develop each factor, craving is given up; when craving is given up, deeds are given up; when deeds are given up, suffering is given up (2.2-2.4, 2.6-2.9). Needs a pattern for chains of ending, which dependent origination will also need. Also the description of each factor as 'abundant, expansive, limitless, and free of ill will' (2.1, 2.5)." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.26/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.27 a dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.27 Taṇhānirodhasutta — The Cessation of Craving"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "The seven factors are the path that leads to the cessation of craving (1.1, 1.4, 2.3); the list (1.6); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.2)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.27/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.41 a dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.41 Vidhāsutta — Discriminations"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "All ascetics and brahmins, past, future and present, who give up the three discriminations do so by developing the seven factors (1.2-1.4, 1.7-1.9); the list (1.6). The sutta doesn't name the three discriminations, so neither does the ontology." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.41/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.49 a dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.49 Ajjhattikaṅgasutta — Interior"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Of interior factors, nothing gives rise to the seven awakening factors like rational application of mind (1.1); one accomplished in it can expect to develop and cultivate them (1.2), by the stock formula (1.3-1.6). Corrected 2026-11-15: 1.2-1.6 had been called abbreviated; 1.2, 1.3 and 1.6 are untranslated in the English but given in the Pali, and 1.4-1.5 give the formula with the Pali's own abbreviation (…pe…) for the middle factors (D19; refined after the re-check audit)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.49/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.50 a dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.50 Bāhiraṅgasutta — Exterior"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Of exterior factors, nothing gives rise to the seven awakening factors like good friendship (1.1); one with good friends can expect to develop and cultivate them (1.2), by the stock formula (1.3-1.6). Corrected 2026-11-15: 1.2-1.6 had been called abbreviated; 1.2, 1.3 and 1.6 are untranslated in the English but given in the Pali, and 1.4-1.5 give the formula with the Pali's own abbreviation (…pe…) for the middle factors (D19; refined after the re-check audit). The chapter's summary verse (2.0-2.4) is not a teaching." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.50/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.7 a dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.7 Kūṭāgārasutta — A Bungalow"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:FullyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "Developing the seven factors slants, slopes and inclines to extinguishment (1.2, 2.4); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.3). The simile of a bungalow's rafters inclining to the peak (1.1; D22)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.7/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

